<title>FRANCE: Algeria's insurance fund expects $1.8 bln receipts.</title>
<headline>Algeria's insurance fund expects $1.8 bln receipts.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria's state insurance fund expects 100 billion dinars ($1.8 billion) in receipts in 1996 from 57 billion ($1.0 billion) in 1995, the official Algerian news agency APS said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The fund, which collects social insurance from private and state-owned enterprises for their employees, is preparing to finalise its book for 1996, said APS quoting the fund head Abdelmajid Bennacer.</p>
<p>The results are expected to be released soon, the agency added but gave no other details.</p>
<p>($1= 56 dinars)</p>
</text>
